# Deny by default: a file enters the index only because a rule below names it.
#
# The usual shape of this file is the opposite - track everything, list the
# junk - and it fails in one direction only: whatever nobody thought to list
# gets committed. Build output, caches, downloaded browsers, an agent's
# scratch file and a stray secret all arrive the same way, and they arrive
# silently. Denying first means the failure lands on the other side: something
# that should be tracked is not, which `git status` shows and a build catches.
#
# To add a file type, add it to section 3. To add one file, add it to section 4.

# --- 1. deny everything -----------------------------------------------------
*

# --- 2. but descend into directories ---------------------------------------
# Without this, git never looks inside a directory and no rule below can match.
!*/

# --- 3. directories that never enter the index ------------------------------
# A file inside an excluded directory cannot be re-included, so these hold
# regardless of the allow rules that follow.
/.cache/
/.tools/
/.vite/
/coverage/
/services/*/bin/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
**/blob-report/
**/sessions/
**/users/
# Scratch space. The allow rules below are extension based, so a note left
# in one of these would otherwise be tracked for being Markdown.
/tmp/
/scratch/
/.scratch/

# --- 4. tracked file types --------------------------------------------------
!*.go
!*.mod
!*.sum
!*.work
!*.ts
!*.tsx
!*.css
!*.html
!*.json
!*.md
!*.mk
!*.sh
!*.txt
!*.yaml
!*.yml
!*.allow

# --- 5. tracked files named individually ------------------------------------
# No extension, or an extension that is not tracked wholesale.
!/Makefile
# Git hooks have no extension by design - git looks them up by name. The
# directory exists only to hold them, so everything in it is tracked.
!/harness/githooks/*
# Redocly loads a custom plugin as JS, not TypeScript; .js is not tracked
# wholesale (the rest of the workspace writes TypeScript), so this one file
# is named individually.
!/harness/quality/redocly/enum-labels.js
!/.gitignore
!/.npmrc
!/.env

# --- 6. exceptions inside the allowed types ---------------------------------
# Local environment overrides are per-machine; only the committed .env above
# is shared (it holds NO_COLOR=1, see DECISIONS.md).
/.env.*
!/.env.example
*.tsbuildinfo
# The brainstorming notes that preceded PRODUCT.md. Kept on disk for reference,
# not tracked: their decisions are already in PRODUCT.md, in English, and a
# second copy would go stale.
/docs/requirements.md
# Per-developer Claude Code overrides; the shared config is .claude/settings.json.
/.claude/settings.local.json
# Compiled Go test binaries (`go test -c`) have no extension and would
# otherwise fall through section 5 only if named there - listed for clarity.
*.test
